   "gap": "Reconstruct Fisher 1922's estimation, information and sufficiency presentation completely with exact regularity conditions: (a) the Type IV/VII and Type II form-parameter calculation of pp.351-355 (four-parameter Hessian of -L in (m,a,nu,r), its Type VII 2x2 split, limit variances of the optimum and moment (beta1,beta2) estimates of nu and r, the tabulated efficiencies and the 80 per cent points r=17.2 and r=14.1) is explicitly not reconstructed (body 1208-1225); (b) the efficiency contours of figs.3-4 on the Types I/II side (y>0) of the normal point are not shown and rest on Fisher alone (body 1129-1132); (c) the proof of thm:p15-w02b-p15-057-contours replaces the rational-function identities N_i/D_i by the claim that they are verified by expanding N_iD_i'-N_i'D_i to zero, without written steps (annex 1694-1721); (d) Fisher's Type III (chi-square) sampling law for chi^2 and 2L with n'-1 degrees of freedom after fitting (pp.357-358) is neither proved nor corrected ('not asserted here', body 1461-1465); (e) Fisher's claim that from p=1 downward the end point determines location with weight growing faster than n is left not settled at p=1 (body 1318-1326), and the zero efficiency of the mean at end exponent 1 is not established (body 1162-1165); (f) Fisher's attribution of the efficiency of mu3, mu4 near the normal point is supported only as an explanation, not proved or corrected (body 1280-1284); (g) the fixed-phase grouped information periodic remainder is bounded only to O(a^3), which does not decide the eighth-order terms of thm:p15-fg-expansion at a fixed phase nor Fisher's 'less than one per cent' small-bin statement (body 1407-1414; host fisher-grouping-and-moments 350-360).",
